## Execution Instructions (per phase)

For each file in the phase:
1. Read the file in full using `XcodeRead`
2. Add a top-of-file `///` overview block immediately before the first `import` (or after the copyright header if one exists) — use a `/// # FileName` heading followed by a summary paragraph
3. Add `///` documentation to every:
   - `struct`, `class`, `enum`, `protocol`, `typealias`
   - `enum case`
   - Stored and computed `var`/`let` properties
   - `func` and `init` declarations (include `- Parameters:`, `- Returns:`, `- Throws:` as applicable)
4. Refine existing `//` inline comments inside method bodies to be more precise where they are vague or missing context
5. After editing, run `XcodeRefreshCodeIssuesInFile` to confirm no compilation errors were introduced

## Verification
After each phase: run `BuildProject` to confirm no regressions before proceeding to next phase.

## Notes
- Do not change any logic or behavior — documentation only
- Preserve all existing `//` comments; add to or replace them only where refinement improves clarity
- Use concrete units in parameter docs (Hz, dB, ms, mm, g) where applicable
- For physics formulas, render the equation in a fenced code block or inline math description
- Mark deprecated/legacy enum cases with `/// - Warning: Deprecated.` and `@available(*, deprecated)`-style notes

